{
  "headline": "Divalproex sodium is not on FDA's shortage list as of 2026-10-21; the label for the product we hold names Coupler LLC, a repack plant with multiple OAI inspections and a 2020-09-15 Warning Letter",
  "headline_cites": ["D2", "E11", "E4", "E6", "E7", "E10"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA's drug shortage list does not include divalproex sodium as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["D2"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale General holds 209 tablets of the 500 mg presentation, which at 8.1 tablets per day provides 25.7 days on hand.",
      "cites": ["D1"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The product label (NDC 67046164703) identifies Coupler LLC as the repack plant (FEI 3003734940).",
      "cites": ["E11"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspection records for that plant show OAI classifications on 2018-04-27, 2020-03-10, and 2021-08-12, with a Warning Letter issued on 2020-09-15.",
      "cites": ["E4", "E6", "E7", "E10"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The most recent inspection (2026-03-02) was classified VAI.",
      "cites": ["E9"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The ranked alternate manufacturer option is to buy from Atlantic Biologicals Corp., which is not on FDA's shortage list today and whose label names no plant we could place.",
      "cites": ["D3"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Because the drug is not listed as short, the buyer should verify current allocation status with Atlantic Biologicals Corp. and monitor FDA inspection updates for Coupler LLC.",
      "cites": ["D2", "D3", "E9"]
    }
  ]
}
